  "body": " String.valueOf()   Evaluate each of the following expressions. Use quote marks to distinguish strings (\"100\") from numbers (100).    String.valueOf(45)     String.valueOf (128-7)     String.valueOf('X')          Correct. The number 45 is converted into the string \"45\".      Incorrect. Did you remember to put quotes around strings?        Correct. The number 121 is converted into the string \"121\"      Incorrect. Did you remember to put quotes around strings?        Correct. The character 'X' is converted to the string \"X\".      Incorrect. Did you remember to put quotes around strings?.       The String.valueOf() method converts its argument into a string.    (a) 45 , (b) 121 , (c) X   "
