  "title": "Newspaper sales.",
  "body": " Newspaper sales   This programming problem has three parts:    Suppose you're going to keep track of the daily newspaper sales at the local kiosk. Declare a two-dimensional array of int .    Write a code segment to initialize each array element to a random value between 50 and two hundred.    Write a code segment to calculate and print the average number of newspapers sold on Sundays. Assume that Sunday is the last day of the week.     public class Newspapers { public static void main(String[] args) { \/\/ Declare a 52 x 7 int array \/\/ Initialize the array with random integers between 50 and 200. \/\/ Calculate and print the average Sunday sales. } }   To generate random integers between 50 and 200, use: 50 + (int)(Math.random()*150)     public class Newspapers { public static void main(String[] args) { \/\/ Declare a 52 x 7 int array int sales[][] = new int[52][7]; \/\/ Initialize the array with random integers between 50 and 200. for (int k = 0; k < sales.length; k++) for (int j= 0; j < sales[k].length; j++) sales[k][j] = 50 + (int)(Math.random() * 150); \/\/ Calculate and print the average Sunday sales. int sum = 0; for (int i=0;i < 52; i++) { sum += sales[i][6]; } System.out.println(\"Sunday avg = \" + sum\/52); } }   "
