  "title": "EFFECTIVE DESIGN: Generality.",
  "body": " EFFECTIVE DESIGN: Generality  Defining a data collection, such as an array or a ArrayList , in terms of the Object class makes it capable of storing and processing any type of value, including values of primitive data types. This is because the Object class is the root of the Java class hierarchy.  "
